    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d766">

                <pb facs="1047" n="927" xml:id="pg927"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2786b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Herrick</hi>)<anchor n="15" xml:id="d766-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-27T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>341. Department’s 339 via London.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d766-f2"/></p>
                <p>Advise Foreign Office informally that the American representatives on the
                    Interallied Committee at Vladivostok and the Technical Board at Harbin have now
                    been instructed to arrange with their colleagues for the immediate cessation of
                    further activities and the earliest possible winding up of the affairs of those
                    two organizations and that the American Minister at Peking has been instructed
                    to present the following note to the Chinese Foreign Office on October 31.</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of note contained in telegram no. 253, Oct. 27, to the
                    Minister in China, printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>The text of the note will be given to the press at Washington on the same
                    day.</p>
                <p>Express the hope that similar instructions will be given to the French
                    representatives in time to assure complete concert of action.</p>
                <p>Repeat to London as Department’s 327 and Rome as Department’s 157 for similar
                    action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d766-f1" n="15" type="source" xml:id="d766-f1-content">
                <p>See last paragraph for instructions to repeat to Rome as no. 157.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d766-f2" n="16" xml:id="d766-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 323, Oct. 26, to the Ambassador in Great Britain, <ref
                        target="#pg923">p. 923</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
